1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
In 4 minutes, one man scored the most famous handball in World Cup history…

2
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:05,600
…and the greatest goal.

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:09,600
June 22, 1986. Mexico City.

4
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:12,400
Argentina against England, in the quarter-final.

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:16,500
51 minutes. A looping ball drops towards England’s goalkeeper.

6
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:20,400
Diego Maradona jumps… and punches it in with his hand.

7
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:21,900
The goal stands.

8
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:25,500
Maradona later said it was scored… “a little with the hand of God.”

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,600
4 minutes later, he picks up the ball in his own half.

10
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:30,800
He turns… and runs.

11
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:34,400
Past one England player. Then another. And another.

12
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:36,700
Around the goalkeeper… and in.

13
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:40,500
In 2002, a FIFA online poll voted it the Goal of the Century.

14
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,400
Argentina won 2–1… and went on to win the World Cup.

15
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:47,900
Cheat, or genius? Tell me in the comments.
